Description: tests: check frame packing BSFs independently of decoder side data
 Read the emitted SEI syntax and NAL placement directly and compare the
 output with FATE references. Cover every layout and content
 interpretation, packet and option precedence, explicit physical eyes,
 unspecified temporal views, flush, replacement and removal. Check
 extracted packet side data, unchanged encoded bytes, cancellation,
 unsupported interpretations and 2D. Check that flushing also restores
 the first-access-unit seek point for display_orientation.
 .
 Require extract_extradata for the API test and its FATE entries. The
 H.264 orientation checks need parameter sets from extradata.
 .
 Also check, with messages written by the test itself: arrangements of
 another id that stay in force, a cancellation that ends one, and a
 layout followed by 2D; extraction of mirrored and quincunx layouts;
 removal from the extradata and from new extradata side data; tile format
 sizes and the self-contained flags. Two more entries use hevc/food.hevc,
 whose VPS and SPS declare general_non_packed_constraint_flag, and
 hevc-conformance/TSCL_A_VIDYO_5.bit, whose pictures are on four temporal
 sublayers.
 .
